{"sourceSha256": "bdbc14e0dbb51e1edab9c57c435211dd820282129d4fc3f51acc8a1ad38913e5", "text": "Dear Doctor,\n\nRe: Miss Ling Wu DOB 01/03/2001\n\nlam writing to update you on the condition of your patient, Ling Wu who is recovering from\n\ninjuries received in a traffic accident one month ago.\n\nLing was initially admitted to hospital via ambulance after a cycling accident on 08/04/19,\nwhich led to an emergency above-knee amputation due to an open tibial-fibular fracture.\nRegarding post-operative management, morphine was used to control operative pain, and\n\nFragmin was administered subcutaneously to prevent deep vein thrombosts.\n\nDuring hospitalisation, Isobel has made good progress physically and the amputation incision\nsite is intact with no signs of infection and the sutures have been removed. Ling is able to\nwrap her amputated limb with an ACE bandage. In terms of mobility, she is able to transfer\n\nindependently and walk unassisted with a rolling walker.\n\nWith regard to her mental state, she has experienced phantom limb pain and insomnia,\nalong with signs of anxiety, silent rumination and decreased interest in social activities.\nTherefore, please monitor for signs of PTSD and arrange a trauma focused CBT programme if\n\nwarranted.\n\nOn discharge, Ling is able to self-administer her medication which includes Neurontin,\nparacetamol, tramadol and amitriptyline. Please note. a follow-up visit at the trauma clinic\n\nhas been scheduled for 17/05/19.\n\n| would appreciate it if you could take over her care and provide ongoing health\n\nmanagement.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nOrthopaedic Surgeon", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Doctor,\n\nRe: Miss Ling Wu DOB 01/03/2001\n\nlam writing to update you on the condition of your patient, Ling Wu who is recovering from\n\ninjuries received in a traffic accident one month ago.\n\nLing was initially admitted to hospital via ambulance after a cycling accident on 08/04/19,\nwhich led to an emergency above-knee amputation due to an open tibial-fibular fracture.\nRegarding post-operative management, morphine was used to control operative pain, and\n\nFragmin was administered subcutaneously to prevent deep vein thrombosts.\n\nDuring hospitalisation, Isobel has made good progress physically and the amputation incision\nsite is intact with no signs of infection and the sutures have been removed. Ling is able to\nwrap her amputated limb with an ACE bandage. In terms of mobility, she is able to transfer\n\nindependently and walk unassisted with a rolling walker.\n\nWith regard to her mental state, she has experienced phantom limb pain and insomnia,\nalong with signs of anxiety, silent rumination and decreased interest in social activities.\nTherefore, please monitor for signs of PTSD and arrange a trauma focused CBT programme if\n\nwarranted.\n\nOn discharge, Ling is able to self-administer her medication which includes Neurontin,\nparacetamol, tramadol and amitriptyline. Please note. a follow-up visit at the trauma clinic\n\nhas been scheduled for 17/05/19.\n\n| would appreciate it if you could take over her care and provide ongoing health\n\nmanagement.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nOrthopaedic Surgeon", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2170.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Doctor,", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Doctor,", "x": 0.0106, "y": 0.00857, "width": 0.12811, "height": 0.01607, "confidence": 0.962, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.0106, "width": 0.04839, "confidence": 0.963}, {"text": "Doctor,", "x": 0.0659, "width": 0.07281, "confidence": 0.961}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Re: Miss Ling Wu DOB 01/03/2001", "lines": [{"text": "Re: Miss Ling Wu DOB 01/03/2001", "x": 0.01106, "y": 0.0475, "width": 0.35023, "height": 0.01571, "confidence": 0.963, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.01106, "width": 0.03041, "confidence": 0.959}, {"text": "Miss", "x": 0.05023, "width": 0.04286, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "Ling", "x": 0.10138, "width": 0.041